content:
The failing orders all come from supplier "Red Sea Parts" starting at t=458, and the invoice_text shows a truncated/different format ("Amount: NNN..." without VAT/total fields visible). No config change is evident. This points to a bad_input change from this specific supplier rather than a sync-job issue — the sync-job deploy timing is coincidental. Let me verify by checking whether all over-budget orders are from Red Sea Parts and what the full invoice text looks like vs baseline orders.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT o.supplier, COUNT(*) as cnt, MIN(o.created_at) as first_seen FROM orders o JOIN messages m ON m.order_id = o.id WHERE m.attempts > 3 GROUP BY o.supplier UNION ALL SELECT o.supplier, COUNT(*) as cnt, MIN(o.created_at) as first_seen FROM orders o JOIN messages m ON m.order_id = o.id WHERE m.attempts <= 3 AND o.created_at >= 300 GROUP BY o.supplier ORDER BY 1",
      "why": "Confirm whether retry-budget violations are exclusively from Red Sea Parts, and whether other suppliers' orders are processing fine — this separates a supplier-specific bad_input from a systemic fault."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "worker",
      "kind": "bad_input",
      "mechanism": "Invoices from supplier 'Red Sea Parts' started arriving in an unexpected layout around t=458, which invoice-agent cannot parse, causing repeated extraction failures and retry budget exhaustion in the worker.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E3", "E4", "E13"],
      "refuting": ["E5"],
      "explains": ["I6_retry_budget"],
      "repair_plan": []
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All retry-budget violations are tied to 'Red Sea Parts' invoices with an unexpected layout arriving from t=458 onward, indicating a bad_input change from that supplier rather than any internal deploy or config issue."
}
```
